  "facts": [
    {
      "id": "refusal-routing",
      "claim": "An InvocationError carries the reason llmgw-core read in a refusal, and a 402 is billing whatever it says. A billing refusal is failover-eligible and counts against the provider's circuit, and a refusal of a request's shape (context overflow, unsupported tools or media) is failover-eligible without counting; neither is retried, a 429 included, and a billing refusal is not reported as throttling. The OpenAI-compatible, Anthropic, Azure OpenAI, Google, Ollama and companion daemon facades keep the reason with the refusal's status and message, and the gateway's own Google transport reads exhausted prepaid credits as billing. Every endpoint chain, the native Messages chain included, decides through the same predicates.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/providers/provider.go; go/internal/providers/error_classification.go; go/internal/providers/openai_compatible_failure.go; go/internal/providers/anthropic_failure.go; go/internal/providers/azure_failure.go; go/internal/providers/google_provider.go; go/internal/providers/googleai.go; go/internal/providers/ollama.go; go/internal/providers/extension_failure.go; go/internal/router/failover_test.go; go/internal/router/classification_parity_test.go; go/internal/api/anthropic_test.go"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "principal-listing",
      "claim": "GET /admin/api/principals answers a page of principals, by name unless sort and order ask otherwise, chosen by id and kind, each repeatable, status, project_id and a search q, with limit 1 to 200 (50 by default), offset and the total its filters select; it calls adminAuthed before anything else. iam.ListPrincipals, which listed every principal, is removed.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/api/principal_list.go; go/internal/api/iam.go; go/internal/iam/principal_list.go; go/internal/iam/repository.go; go/internal/api/principal_list_test.go; go/internal/iam/principal_list_test.go"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "admin-state",
      "claim": "handleState calls adminAuthed before anything else, and its answer no longer carries keys or principals. It carries counts (keys, principals, active_principals, active_humans, project_owners) and default_owner, the first active person by name, and its other fields are those v1.8.0 answers.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/api/admin.go; go/internal/iam/principal_list.go; go/internal/api/principal_list_test.go"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "names-on-rows",
      "claim": "Listed project memberships carry principal_name, principal_kind and principal_status; provider connections, open circuits, alert rules and outbox deliveries carry principal_name. The key listing takes grant, a name a key's allowed routes or allowed models hold, and the status unrevoked.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "go/internal/iam/models.go; go/internal/iam/repository.go; go/internal/iam/connections.go; go/internal/iam/alerts.go; go/internal/iam/key_list.go; go/internal/api/key_list.go; go/internal/api/provider_status.go; go/internal/api/circuit_status_test.go; go/internal/iam/alerts_test.go; go/internal/iam/oauth_test.go; go/internal/iam/key_list_test.go; go/internal/api/key_list_test.go"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "console",
      "claim": "The console reads no key or principal list from the state. Owner and principal pickers search the principal listing a page at a time and name a chosen principal the page does not list by asking for it; key pickers search the key listing. Access pages its principal table on the server, a project's page pages its keys, and renaming a route counts the keys that grant the old name on the server. Names come from the rows that carry principal IDs, counts from the state's counts, and the default catalog owner from default_owner. Z.ai, ModelScope and NEAR AI Cloud show their marks, regional and variant entries share their provider's, and the Providers page shelves entries by the registry's categories, placing LiteLLM, vLLM and LM Studio under Local & self-hosted. The committed bundle is rebuilt: dist/assets/index-WbiKL91W.js replaces index-DuO9dpX1.js, and the stylesheet is the one v1.8.0 embeds.",
      "status": "observed",
      "evidence": {
        "source": "git diff --name-status v1.8.0..HEAD -- go/internal/web/console"
      }
    },
